 <shortdesc>Complex Multiply FP16 Values</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1045992">
   <string>This instruction performs a complex multiply operation. There are normal and complex conjugate forms of the oper&#173;ation. The broadcasting and masking for this operation is done on 32-bit quantities representing a pair of FP16 values.</string></para>
  <para unique="1045993">
   <string>Rounding is performed at every FMA (fused multiply and add) boundary. Execution occurs as if all MXCSR excep&#173;tions are masked. MXCSR status bits are updated to reflect exceptional conditions.</string></para>
  </longdesc>
